/-- **Stacks Tag 0C22.** Let `R → S` be a flat ring map of Noetherian rings. If `R` is a normal
ring and every fibre ring `κ(𝔭) ⊗_R S` is a normal ring, then `S` is a normal ring. -/
@[stacks 0C22 "The ring map is an `Algebra R S` instance with `Module.Flat R S`, and the fibre \
  ring `S ⊗_R κ(𝔭)` is Mathlib's `Ideal.Fiber 𝔭 S`, as in the companion statements 0C21 and 0339. \
  Normality is the library's `IsNormalRing` (Definition 00GV), definitionally the `IsDomain` plus \
  `IsIntegrallyClosed` condition on `Localization.AtPrime 𝔮` that tags 030C(1), 031S and 033G \
  write out, and the fibre hypothesis is normality, not geometric normality. Mathlib has neither \
  a normal-ring predicate nor this ascent. See the module docstring.", ega "IV 6.5.4"
    "(ii), affine case"]
public theorem isNormalRing_of_flat_of_isNormalRing_fiber {R : Type u} {S : Type v} [CommRing R]
    [CommRing S] [Algebra R S] [IsNoetherianRing R] [IsNoetherianRing S] [Module.Flat R S]
    (hR : IsNormalRing R) (hfibre : ∀ (p : Ideal R) [p.IsPrime], IsNormalRing (p.Fiber S)) :
    IsNormalRing S :=
  Stacks.Flatness.NormalFibreAscent.solution hR hfibre

end
